00:18:39.180 --> 00:18:47.040
Like, was the game, was the game building on anything here or is it, does it feel like it's just the background changes between levels?

00:18:47.040 --> 00:18:57.420
I was surprised that throughout most of the game, uh, you can fight back with almost all of the, um, missile projectiles, especially for some of the bosses.

00:18:57.420 --> 00:19:02.840
That was like nice to be able to like fire those things away rather than forcibly dodge them.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:13.360
Um, I think it does provide some, um, some light spins on, on like what we've seen in shmups, even if it is just a pretty standard, um, a shmup.

00:19:13.360 --> 00:19:20.900
But the, the level to level really did just feel like a, uh, a palette, uh, swap for me.

00:19:21.200 --> 00:19:31.740
Not, not even like, yes, the backgrounds are more intricate, but the locations even kind of don't really change in extreme ways where like it makes any sense of like, oh, we're, we're getting somewhere.

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:36.020
Like it just kind of is taking you to different landscapes and then all of a sudden you're in a computer hall.

00:19:36.220 --> 00:19:37.720
It's very nice wallpaper.

00:19:38.480 --> 00:19:52.180
Um, and because it's wallpaper, like it'd be cool if there was, if it actually felt like a place that you were driving through that had like variations in, uh, what you're seeing from like screen to screen.

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:55.760
Uh, and not just level to level, but no, it's just wallpaper.

00:19:56.040 --> 00:19:59.620
There's no, like, there's nothing environmental going on.

00:19:59.620 --> 00:20:04.960
And I think they really missed an opportunity to differentiate themselves.

00:20:05.280 --> 00:20:15.120
Like most shmups have been able to differentiate themselves, which is in boss design, where these are just sort of like vehicles that vaguely look futuristic.

00:20:15.660 --> 00:20:17.300
And that's it.

00:20:17.720 --> 00:20:23.860
With the boss designs, I can like picture like a, like a Rorschach test version of each of these bosses.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:30.540
And they're all kind of just like these like vague, like pixelized machinery things.

00:20:31.160 --> 00:20:36.840
Yes. Like they do not stand out in any way to me as like, oh yeah, there's the, the, this boss or the, that boss.

00:20:36.980 --> 00:20:41.240
It's all just like, oh, pieces of machinery with weak spots floating around in different ways.

00:20:41.900 --> 00:20:46.540
Um, and, and, you know, as far as the backgrounds, they're very pretty backgrounds, but yeah, I agree.

00:20:46.540 --> 00:20:52.680
They, they didn't really like tie into, tie into the progression too much.

